```javascript
const axios = require('axios'); // Make sure to install 'axios' package first: `npm install axios`

async function postMessageToSlackChannel(text, channel) {
  try {
    const options = {
      method: 'post',
      url: `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage`,
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN}`, // Replace with your bot token
      },
      data: {
        channel,
        text,
      },
    };

    await axios(options);
    console.log(`Successfully posted message: "${text}" to channel "${channel}"`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error posting message to Slack: ${error}`);
  }
}

// Usage example:
postMessageToSlackChannel('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

This example uses the `axios` library to make HTTP requests and simplifies the process of sending messages to Slack. The `postMessageToSlackChannel` function accepts two arguments - `text` and `channel`. It then constructs an options object containing the necessary configuration for making the POST request, sets up authentication using a bot token, and sends the message using `axios`. If the request is successful, it logs a success message; otherwise, it logs an error message.

