 Sure thing! Here's a PHP function called `smart_sort_array` that should meet your requirements:

```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') {
    $size = count($set);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $size - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $size - $i - 1; $j++) {
            if (($order == 'ASC' && $set[$j]['age'] > $set[$j+1]['age']) || ($order == 'DESC' && $set[$j]['age'] < $set[$j+1]['age'])) {
                // Swap elements
                $temp = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $set[$j+1];
                $set[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $set;
}
```

This function takes in two parameters: `$set`, which is an array of associative arrays as described, and `$order` which defaults to 'ASC' for ascending order. The function uses a simple implementation of bubble sort algorithm to sort the elements based on their age keys. If you want to sort in descending order, pass 'DESC' as the second argument. Let me know if this helps or if you have any questions!

